# The assessment of AGT-EXEC-001 against this build. The requirement identifier is this
# file's stem and appears nowhere inside it, because a second place to spell the identity
# is a second place for it to be wrong -- the rule OD-SPEC-007 chose for a record
# registration, and CHK-003.assessment states for this registry.
#
# AGT-EXEC-001: "Agent capabilities shall be partitioned into read, propose, preview,
# mutate, execute, approve, and publish classes with separate authorization and audit
# requirements."
#
# The prior audit (P13-TRACE-AGT-EXEC-AUDIT) left this Unassessed, finding no legitimate
# site. Re-checked directly: `AuthorityClass` (`nomos-contracts`) is a real, deliberately
# designed enum partitioning agent capability into exactly the seven classes this
# requirement names -- Read, Propose, Preview, Mutate, Execute, Approve, Publish, verbatim
# -- and `Requires_Explicit_Grant` gives a real, if binary, per-class authorization
# distinction. It was simply never cited before now.
#
# At the time of that re-check, no operation anywhere in the live workspace actually
# carried or was checked against `AuthorityClass` -- zero consumers outside its own
# declaring module. `nomos_corrections`' own Stage -> Validate -> Commit -> Rollback
# lifecycle structurally parallels `MutationClass` (Preview -> Validate -> Apply ->
# Rollback) almost exactly, and each of its real, tested lifecycle types (`Preview`,
# `StagedPlan`, `ValidatedPlan`, `CommittedPlan`) now names its own `Mutation_Class`,
# and `CommittedPlan::ROLLBACK_MUTATION_CLASS` names `Rollback`'s -- the first real
# consumer `AuthorityClass`/`MutationClass` have had anywhere, closing the corrections
# half of this requirement's own "partitioned into classes" clause down to the
# operational level: `value.Mutation_Class().Required_Authority()` is a real,
# tested, queryable `AuthorityClass` for a real operation today, not merely a type that
# happens to exist. This is declared metadata carried alongside each value, the same
# shape `CorrectionCandidate::Class`/`Labels` and `ValidatedPlan::Commit`'s `Evidence`
# parameter already establish for this crate -- not an enforcement gate that refuses a
# call lacking the right authority, which is the real remaining half of "separate
# authorization ... requirements".
#
# `Claim` (`nomos-ledger`, the concrete shape an agent's run already takes here, per
# AGT-EXEC-002's own committed assessment) still carries who holds an item and when the
# lease lapses, nothing about which class the held work exercises -- deliberately not
# touched by this build, since `Claim` is serialized into the shared, concurrently-held
# `work/ledger.json` and a schema change there risks corrupting another live session's
# read of the whole board, a different hazard than the population-of-zero caution
# `OD-ROADMAP-001` retires. `VerificationRecord` is likewise untouched for the same
# reason, and still has no counterpart for Propose/Approve/Publish, which have no
# implemented operation at all. "Separate authorization and audit requirements" has real,
# queryable operational reality for corrections' Preview/Validate/Apply/Rollback classes
# now; it remains type-level only for the ledger-claim half of an agent's run, and
# unbuilt entirely for Propose/Approve/Publish.
verdict: Partial
